<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33532" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλεγος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>song, melody</i>, orig.
			accompanied by the flute, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλυρος
			ἔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				185
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				146
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσίας ἔ. ἰήϊος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
					3(1)i
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				ii9
			</span></i>; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔλεγοι</span>, title of a
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος αὐλῳδικός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1132d
			</span></i>; of the <i>song</i> of the nightingale, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				218
			</span></i>(pl.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλεγον οἶτον</span>, of
			the halcyon, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1091
			</span></i> (lyr.); later, <i>lament, song of mourning</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.782
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>poem in elegiac distichs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				121
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱλαροὶ ἔ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				10.19
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>). (Commonly derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἒ ἒ
				λέγειν</span>, to cry woe! woe! <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				326.49
			</span></i>.)</div>
